speechtext:
The first part of this subclause seems to be the same as found in the definition in the Exportation of Power and Fluids and Importation of the Gas Act but part 2 of the subclause seems to be entirely new. It reads:
(ii) with reference to oil, to bring oil into Canada through pipe lines, by railway tank car, by tank truck or by tanker;
This does not appear to cover the question of oil transported by aircraft, by barges or in oil drums. The amount transported by aircraft I should think would be very small but transportation by barges or in oil drums may be considerable. Would it be possible to make a small amendment to include the words "by any other means"?
